      "content": "I won’t pretend there’s a quick fix or some silver lining to hand you — that’d be a lie and you deserve more than lies. What I can tell you is that being tired is real, and it doesn’t make you weak; it makes you aware of how heavy you’ve been carrying this alone. You don’t have to perform hope for me or anyone else. Just breathe for the next minute, and if you can, tell me one thing — anything — that isn’t about the ash.",
